+## Story 10.6 residual risk
+
+`QuickCheckScenarioTest.sequences that leave the observed faces unchanged` reported “Observed-face-preserving sequences: 44 of 123500; residual aliases of a match: 1”. The seeded JVM scenario found one alias among all 123,500 sequences (0.00081%), or 1 of 44 among sequences that changed the cube while preserving the observed faces. The alias was `R U2 R'` with plan faces {B, D}: a match outside the candidate model (length > 2) that the Partial check reports as VERIFIED. Regenerated on 2026-11-18 with `./gradlew :core:domain:test --tests '*QuickCheckScenarioTest' -i`. This is a scenario result with a fixed seed and sequence depth. [QuickCheckScenarioTest](../../core/domain/src/test/kotlin/dev/cubentia/domain/tutor/QuickCheckScenarioTest.kt)
+
+Recommendation on the residual risk — PO decision, device session C.
+
+## Fixture accuracy
+
+The product Kotlin pipeline scored 432/432 sticker reads on the A2 fixtures, with zero confidently wrong and three uncertain. Seven of eight reads were both correct and valid because one fixture's truth is invalid. The center-pixel input scored 646/648 with two confidently wrong. The OQ-4 prototype live-baseline block reports 645/648 overall and 237/240 for independently entered truth. These fixture samples cover studio lighting. [Product pipeline accuracy](../scan-accuracy.md) · [OQ-4 live baseline](oq-4-guided-scan.md#live-baseline)
+
+## Release recommendations
+
+| Flow | OFF / BETA / GA |
+| --- | --- |
+| Guided 6-face Scan | PO decision — device session C |
+| Quick Scan | PO decision — device session C |
+| Quick Check | PO decision — device session C |
+| Placement | PO decision — device session C |
+| Case recognition | PO decision — device session C |
+
+## Manual fallback
+
+- [ ] Guided 6-face Scan — choose Enter colors, enter the stickers manually and verify that the accepted cube reaches Solve.
+- [ ] Quick Scan — trigger an uncertain corner read, finish on the guided grid, then verify that the review can hand off to Enter colors.
+- [ ] Quick Check — produce a result that requests more evidence, then verify that Scan all 6 faces opens the full scan and the Learner can still use the manual path.
+- [ ] Placement — use Enter colors to reach a suggestion, then verify that the Learner can choose another stage or start Stage 1.
+- [ ] Case recognition — use Enter colors from the capture flow, submit a valid cube and verify that the library shows the applicable result.
